{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recording-tree-002-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/RecordingOptimizerTests.cs","line":2204,"method":"CanAutoSplitIgnoringGhostTriggers_AllowsTreeRecordings","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RecordingOptimizer.cs:189-203; add `if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(rec.TreeId)) return false;` -> red","what_it_asserts":"CanAutoSplitIgnoringGhostTriggers returns true for a recording with TreeId set, no part events, and 30 s halves across an Exo->Atmo boundary.","why_weak":"TreeId is never read by CanAutoSplitIgnoringGhostTriggers or anything it calls; without TreeId the fixture still returns true, and base CanAutoSplit also returns true (no trigger events exist), so the cell cannot fail on any tree-specific regression short of adding a new skip. The tree-split contract is actually pinned at pass level by RunOptimizationPass_SplitsMultiEnvRecording (line 2633).","proposed_action":"Assert the real contrast (Assert.True(CanAutoSplit(rec, 1)) to document that no tree gate and no trigger gate exist for this fixture), or delete the cell and leave tree-split coverage to the pass-level test.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recording-tree-002-02","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/RecordingOptimizerTests.cs","line":2349,"method":"FindSplitCandidatesForOptimizer_FindsTreeRecordings","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RecordingOptimizer.cs:629; insert a `if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(rec.TreeId)) continue;` skip -> red","what_it_asserts":"FindSplitCandidatesForOptimizer returns exactly one (0,1) candidate for a TreeId recording crossing ExoBallistic->Atmospheric.","why_weak":"RecordingOptimizer.cs reads TreeId nowhere; the fixture yields the identical candidate with the TreeId line deleted, so the cell reds only on a newly added tree skip and asserts nothing about tree membership, tree topology, or the split pass's tree bookkeeping.","proposed_action":"Drop the inert TreeId (and rename to the boundary it covers), or drive the tree recording through RunOptimizationPass and assert tree membership effects the way RunOptimizationPass_MergeUpdatesTreeMembershipAndBranchParentLinks does for merge.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
{"kind":"finding","id":"F-recording-tree-002-03","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/RecordingOptimizerTests.cs","line":2397,"method":"FindSplitCandidatesForOptimizer_SkipsContinuousEvaSurfaceAtmoSurface","category":"T3","severity":"Low","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RecordingOptimizer.cs:412 and :194; delete BOTH the IsSurfaceGrazePattern call and the ShouldKeepContinuousEvaAtmoSurfaceTogether call -> candidate appears -> red","what_it_asserts":"FindSplitCandidatesForOptimizer returns no candidate for a 3-section Surface->Atmo->Surface recording flagged as continuous EVA.","why_weak":"The surface-graze rule suppresses at RecordingOptimizer.cs:412 before CanAutoSplitIgnoringGhostTriggers ever runs, so the named EVA rule at :194 is not the deciding guard; deleting either guard alone leaves the cell green, and the same Empty result holds with EvaCrewName/ParentRecordingId removed. The graze rule has direct tests at line 5878 and the 2-section EVA gate at line 2373, so the cell adds no isolated coverage.","proposed_action":"Either rename to name the surface-graze pattern it actually pins, or add a control (same fixture without the EVA fields) plus a non-graze EVA fixture (Atmo run over BriefSectionMaxSeconds) to isolate the EVA-continuity gate.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
